######SiB4 Instructions######

####Steps for Running SiB4####
1) Obtain SiB4 from GitLab
      - Open an account for GitLab and ask for permission to SiB4
      - git clone https://USERNAME@gitlab.com/kdhaynes/sib4v2_corral.git

2) Compile SiB4
   - Change to the 'code' directory
   - Edit the Makefile for any necessary computer/system specifications
   - At the prompt, type 'make'
      - Compiles all objects
      - Links necessary files/libraries
      - Creates the executable SiB4D
      - Finishes with the message: "Finished building == SiB4D"

3) Move the executable from the 'code' directory to the main directory

4) Move a namelist containing the simulation specifications into the main directory
   Option 1) Site Simulations
      - Change into the 'info/sites' directory
      - Copy the generic namel_sibdrv file into the main directory
      - Edit the namel_sibdrv file, 
        replacing the XX site identifiers with a specific site

   Option 2) Global Simulations
      - Change into the 'info/global' directory
      - Copy the namel_sibdrv file into the main directory

5) Modify the namel_sibdrv file

6) Change any parameters, if necessary
   + Change to the 'input/params' directory
   + Alter any of the files and variables

7) Change any variables to be output
   + Change to the 'input' directory
   + Alter the first three columns of the 'sib_outopts' file
     to turn the variable output on/off 
     Column 1) True = Output variable in QP files
     Column 2) True = Output variable in PBP files
     Column 3) True = Output variable in HR files

8) If necessary, perform a spin-up simulation to acquire balanced carbon pools
      + Set the 'spinup' flag to true
      + Specify initial pool values (spinup_default)
          -- Zero pools except minimal root pool (spinup_default = .true.)
          -- Restart file values (spinup_default = .false.)
      + Specify whether to save output during the spinup (spinup_output)
      + Specify the number of years to use in the spinup calculation (spinup_numyrs)
          -- If the number of years does not match the start/end times,
              it will loop over the years specified to reach this total number
      + Specify the maximum number of iterations for the spinup (spinup_maxiter)
      + Specify the threshold required to declare pools balanced (spinup_threshold)

      + Run SiB4: In the main directory, type './SiB4D'
      + Save the equilibrium restart file (sib_requib.nc)
      + In the namel_sibdrv file:
         -- Set the initial condition file to the newly-created restart file
         -- Set the spinup flag to 'false'

9) Run SiB4
   + In the main directory, type './SiB4D'

####Notes For SiB4####
- SiB4 can be run using multiple processors
  At the prompt:
  >./SiB4D rank nchunks
    - Rank specifies which process number
    - Nchunks specifies the total number of processes

- SiB4 can be run specifying the location of namel_sibdrv,
  rather than requiring the namelist to be in the same directory
  as the executable
  At the prompt:
  >./SiB4D /directory/namel_sibdrv

